    {
      "title": "TER-MOD Active Room Temperature Sensors (Controllers) with Modbus, datasheet",
      "version": "SN1.416 (07/2024)",
      "date": "2024-07",
      "url": "https://produal-pim.rockon.io/rockon/api/v1/int/extmedia/openFile/01TGWJBKAFJRVSPLMU7BEJBTWG5PLVDYBE",
      "note": "Modbus registers, configuration parameters and notes (pages 11 to 14); file TER-MOD_240710_DS_en.pdf",
      "accessed": "2026-11-24",
      "sha256": "262f52e4403a8ef61ceadec36e10888848dd9c73f2bafa852346987f87a661f4"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Written from the manufacturer's datasheet (07/2024); not tested on a device.",
    "The datasheet is printed with the SyxthSense name; the device is a Produal product.",
    "The sheet lists register numbers from zero (coil 0, input 30001 is address 1, holding 40000 is address 0); some masters add one. The temperature is read from address 1 with function 04. address_base is 0.",
    "Defaults: 9600 bit/s, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit. The address is set with the bit switch (1 to 63) or over the network (1 to 247); the baud rate with the bit switch or over the network when switches 7 and 8 are off. The sheet gives address 1 as the default in the table and 0 in the text; 1 is used here.",
    "Changes made over the network are not stored automatically: write 1 to holding 101 (non volatile memory update). Address and baud rate changes also need a restart.",
    "Temperature, light and the resistive inputs depend on the fitted options (-LCD, -SP, -SPB, -LL, -PB, -PB2, -DI2, -RI2). Temperature values are in degrees Celsius unless holding 39 selects Fahrenheit.",
    "The datasheet gives a value range that does not agree with the configuration tool: the display mode lists setpoint only in the tool, not in the register table. The ranges used are the ones of the register table.",
    "Registers 301-315 repeat the input registers (plus the 0-10 V inputs 314 and 315). They are holding registers (FC03), read only, from firmware 2.25.",
    "The 2015 issue of the datasheet listed coil 7 (reset SPA) and fewer push button registers; the 2018 and 2024 issues, which have the same registers, do not list coil 7, but devices with firmware 2.29 and 2.33 answer it.",
    "The firmware version register (input 100) has no format in the datasheet; devices report 229 and 233 for firmware 2.29 and 2.33, so it is read as the version times 100.",
    "Not tested yet: coils 8 to 11, discrete input 7, holding register 69 and the registers 301-315.",
    "Tested on TER-MOD, firmware 2.29 and 2.33, November 2026."
  ],
